add('N054','G. Simplicial quotients and transfer','The deleted universal-cover claim and its later restricted use',[(35,22),(39,33)],'withdrawn in the same text',r'deleted “universel”; “correspondant à l’image”; “E est … contractile”',r'fundamental|fondamental|revêtement|section|quotient|LM7',r'''Theorem 1 replaces “universel” by the covering corresponding to the image of \(p_*:\pi_1(E)\to\pi_1(B)\), and Theorem 3 later invokes \(E/S\) as universal in its contractible-\(E\) setting. The two statements are connected by the actual quotient projection \(E/S\to E/G\) and the recorded subgroup \(\operatorname{im}p_*\), so the cancellation and later use should be read together.''',r'''LM7 E.23 is Open by the return and concerns continuous section maps of specified arithmetic quotients; these scans add a stabilizer-quotient construction, while the supplied excerpt gives no identification of its \(N\) or its arithmetic section maps with this \(E,G,S\).''',['LM7 E.23'])
add('N055','G. Simplicial quotients and transfer','Two occurrences of B in lifted-path arguments',[(36,24),(36,32)],'reading question',r'“λ une arête de B telle que pλ=β”; “un lacet de B”',r'chemin|path|fundamental|quotient|section',r'''The path-lifting proof calls \(\lambda\) an edge of \(B\) before applying \(p:E\to B\) to it, and the independence argument calls \((\gamma,-\gamma')\) a loop of \(B\) after choosing both paths in \(E\). The candidate reading \(E\) in these two positions is forced as a domain question for the displayed \(p\), but remains a research question because the frozen source writes \(B\).''',r'''Neither the LM7 E.23 excerpt nor MPL_142_001-093 §316 supplies these paths or alternative letters; the former is an open section problem and the latter a bibliography lead, so neither can settle the reading.''',['LM7 E.23','MPL_142_001-093 §316'])
add('N056','G. Simplicial quotients and transfer','The explicit quotient homomorphism chi',[(36,30),(37,22),(37,33)],'unpursued implication',r'“Définition de χ”; “Le noyau de χ contient … S”',r'fundamental|quotient|stabilis|class.two|γ_3|section',r'''The map \(\chi(g)\) is constructed from a path \(x_0\to gx_0\), projected to \(B\) and taken modulo \(\operatorname{im}\pi_1(E)\); the concatenation and stabilizer calculations on scan 037 make its group law explicit. Armstrong’s 1965 Theorem 3 uses the corresponding projected-edge-path map for a simply connected complex, with the fixed-point normal subgroup as kernel [P14]; the comparison requires the manuscript’s realization and covering conventions to be matched to that source.''',r'''This supplies a concrete quotient-map method bearing on LM7 E.23 and INTAKE LM7_CONTINUED §?, but neither excerpt identifies its class-two kernel with the normal closure of stabilizers, and the intake remains an intake reading rather than a referee verdict.''',['LM7 E.23','INTAKE LM7_CONTINUED §?'],['P14'])
add('N057','G. Simplicial quotients and transfer','Testing the assertion that translated simplices are disjoint',[(38,22)],'own idea',r'“donc tout simplexe en un simplexe disjoint”',r'simplex|simplic|quotient|fundamental|topolog',r'''Let \(E\) be the simplicial line with vertices \(\mathbf Z\) and edges \([n,n+1]\), and let \(\tau(n)=n+1\) generate the translation action of \(\mathbf Z\); every vertex stabilizer is trivial, yet \([0,1]\cap\tau[0,1]=\{1\}\). The realization quotient is the covering \(\mathbf R\to\mathbf R/\mathbf Z\), so this example tests the written implication about closed simplices while keeping the quotient map fully explicit. Does “disjoint” refer instead to open simplices, or should the covering argument use sufficiently small stars or a subdivision, as in Armstrong’s treatment [P14]?''',r'''The supplied context has no corresponding simplex argument; its fundamental-group placement in README and the open LM7 E.23 entry gain a specific local proof check, with no conclusion about the arithmetic section problem.''',['LM7 E.23'],['P14'],confidence='high for the intersection calculation; unresolved for the intended meaning of simplexe',reason='The action, stabilizers, intersection, and geometric quotient are explicit; the source does not qualify the word disjoint.')
add('N058','G. Simplicial quotients and transfer','Averaging the lifted chain',[(39,20)],'unproved claim',r'“θ … est un cycle”; “p(θ)=nζ”',r'averag|moyenn|norm|transfer|transfert|norme',r'''Theorem 2 chooses arbitrary lifts \(\tau_i\) of the simplices in a cycle and averages them over \(G\), asserting that the resulting \(\theta\) is a cycle and projects to \(n\zeta\). The proof needs the equality of orbit sums for alternate lifts of a face, so that cancellation in \(\partial\zeta\) lifts to cancellation in \(\partial\theta\); that is the chain-level map behind the claimed image statement.''',r'''MPL_60_036-070 §2 places averaging at 60/037–047, and MPL_11_043-058+56 N045 records a norm-2 annotation at 56/020; the current scan adds an explicit sum over a group action, while neither earlier excerpt supplies its chain complex or identifies its norm with this sum.''',['MPL_60_036-070 §2','MPL_11_043-058+56 N045'])
add('N059','G. Simplicial quotients and transfer','The unfinished homology-to-homotopy step',[(39,33)],'unproved claim / withdrawn in the same text',r'deleted “fini”; “tous les éléments”; ending “les H_i(E/S)”',r'homotop|homolog|torsion|finite|fundamental|section',r'''Theorem 3 deletes finiteness of the higher homotopy group and retains an elementwise prime-support statement involving powers of \(|S|\), then stops at the homology groups of \(E/S\). The missing bridge is a homology-to-homotopy argument for this simply connected quotient, tracking the class of groups killed elementwise by powers of \(|S|\), rather than an unrecorded assertion that the entire homotopy group is finite.''',r'''LM7 E.23 and its intake excerpt concern continuous sections of specified quotients and provide no such homotopy argument; these pages add a topological proof fragment and its local retraction of “fini”, with no resolution of that open entry.''',['LM7 E.23','INTAKE LM7_CONTINUED §?'],flags=['withdrawn'])
add('N060','G. Simplicial quotients and transfer','An explicit abstract-group comparison for the class-two quotient',[(35,22),(37,45)],'own idea',r'“G/S”; “engendré par les stabilisateurs”',r'LM7 E\.23|N/γ_3N|class.two|section|quotient|E\.37',r'''Can the quotient map \(q:N\to N/\gamma_3N\) in the intake be compared with the manuscript after applying the forgetful functor from profinite groups to abstract groups? For \(Q=U(N/\gamma_3N)\), the bar construction \(E_m=Q^{m+1}\), with faces deleting entries and degeneracies repeating them, is contracted by insertion of \(1\); the diagonal \(U(N)\)-action through \(U(q)\) has stabilizer \(\ker U(q)\) at every vertex and quotient \(BQ\). Which continuous or profinite realization, together with the arithmetic marking and section map to E.16, would transport this explicit abstract construction to the actual open problem?''',r'''This is filed under LM7 E.23 [Open, return claim] and INTAKE LM7_CONTINUED §? [intake only], whose cited earlier scans are 172–178 for E.23; LM7_PUSH C.6’s claimed classification is not re-derived, and no arithmetic identification is supplied by these excerpts.''',['LM7 E.23','INTAKE LM7_CONTINUED §?','LM7_PUSH C.6'],confidence='high for the displayed abstract bar construction; low for its proposed arithmetic application',reason='The quotient map and stabilizers are explicit, but forgetting topology supplies no continuous section comparison or arithmetic marking.')

add('N061','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','The trace-one homothety argument',[(42,4),(42,14)],'unproved claim',r'“1=Tr_G b”; “Tr_G φ_M(b)”',r'trace|Tr_|transfer|transfert|averag|norm',r'''The proof sends \(b\in B\) to the homothety \(\varphi_M(b)\) and uses conjugation \(g\varphi_M(b)g^{-1}=\varphi_M(gb)\) to turn a ring trace into a trace of endomorphisms. The omitted cohomological step is the action of that endomorphism trace on the chosen Tate complex, including negative degrees and the semilinear \(B\)-action.''',r'''The averaging lead MPL_60_036-070 §2 and norm annotation MPL_11_043-058+56 N045 (56/020) provide possible comparison targets, while this scan adds the exact ring-to-endomorphism map required before identifying their operations.''',['MPL_60_036-070 §2','MPL_11_043-058+56 N045'])
add('N062','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','Dimension shifting inside semilinear modules',[(42,23)],'unproved claim',r'“On prouve de façon … analogue”; “M⊗_Z Z(G)”',r'dimension.shift|Tate|module|cohomolog|trace|induc',r'''The scan writes the diagonal \(G\)-action and the \(B\)-module structure on \(M\otimes_{\mathbf Z}\mathbf Z(G)\), verifies compatibility, and invokes its Tate acyclicity. The downward shift is only described as analogous; specifying its surjection and kernel in the same semilinear module category would complete the two directions needed for the fixed-degree criterion.''',r'''No context excerpt gives this semilinear resolution; the earlier norm/averaging leads remain relevant only through the homothety and transfer maps in N061.''',['MPL_60_036-070 §2','MPL_11_043-058+56 N045'])
add('N063','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','A concrete norm-two comparison question',[(42,20)],'own idea',r'“l’homothétie λ … est nulle”',r'norm 2|norme|exc\. 2|pairing|trace|averag',r'''For \(G=C_2\) acting trivially on \(B=\mathbf Z\), the trace map is \(b\mapsto2b\), and \(\widehat H^0(C_2,\mathbf Z)=\mathbf Z/2\), on which multiplication by the trace element \(2\) is zero. Can the norm-2 annotation in the earlier package be compared through an explicit map from its coefficient or chain object to such a trace module, so that its displayed pairing and the present annihilator statement can actually be evaluated together?''',r'''The exact lead is MPL_11_043-058+56 N045, at 56/020, whose excerpt records an uncertain target and “exc. 2”; these pages add an explicit trace mechanism, but the missing earlier map prevents an asserted identification of the two norm operations.''',['MPL_11_043-058+56 N045'],confidence='high for the C2 calculation; low for the earlier pairing identification',reason='The trace and Tate quotient are computed directly; the earlier pairing is supplied only as an uncertain excerpt.')
add('N064','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','The ramification corollary and the illegible reference',[(42,2),(42,46)],'unproved claim',r'“e … est inversible dans A”; “Voir … dans le livre de”',r'ramif|inerti|trace|local|norm',r'''The corollary asserts the trace condition from invertibility of the inertia-group order, after inserting integrality, normality and locality assumptions and cancelling a longer formulation. A proof must track the decomposition and inertia subgroups at the chosen maximal ideal and the map \(\operatorname{Tr}:B\to A\); the marginal book reference remains too weak to identify as a citation.''',r'''The context’s local-symbol and norm leads MPL_60_002-035 §2 and MPL_60_036-070 §2 give no statement of this corollary, so its hypotheses and the unresolved marginal reference are additions from this scan.''',['MPL_60_002-035 §2','MPL_60_036-070 §2'])
add('N065','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','Relative trace and stable elements',[(43,2),(43,53)],'reading question',r'“éléments … stables”; “\widehat H(G′,M)^G”',r'stable|transfert|transfer|subgroup|sous.groupe|Sylow',r'''The page assumes \(G'\subset G\) and labels a subgroup of \(\widehat H(G',M)\) by a superscript \(G\), later explaining it as the stable elements. Which family of restriction/conjugation maps through \(G'\cap gG'g^{-1}\) defines that subgroup, and how does it interact with the stated relative corestriction without adding an unwritten normality assumption on \(G'\)?''',r'''MPL_60_036-070 §2 supplies only an averaging lead, and the LM7 excerpts supply particular quotient problems; this scan adds the stable-element terminology and the subgroup/intersection maps needed for any further comparison.''',['MPL_60_036-070 §2','LM7 E.23'])
add('N066','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','The explicitly deferred relative-projectivity lemma',[(43,44)],'self-flagged',r'“\unsure{Reste} à prouver”; “1=Tr_{G/G′} φ”',r'Tr_|trace|transfer|transfert|stable|Reste',r'''The author explicitly leaves to prove the implication from an identity endomorphism expressed as \(\operatorname{Tr}_{G/G'}\varphi\), with \(\varphi\in\operatorname{Hom}_{G'}(M,M)\), to surjective corestriction and injective restriction with stable image. The immediate task is to construct the comparison of the two Tate complexes induced by \(\varphi\), then verify the composite and the double-coset restrictions displayed at the foot of the page.''',r'''No supplied context entry claims this lemma; the nearby averaging lead MPL_60_036-070 §2 gives no replacement proof, so this remains a manuscript-marked verification item.''',['MPL_60_036-070 §2'],flags=['self'])
add('N067','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','The Sylow application and the marginal quotient',[(43,42),(43,55),(43,57)],'reading question',r'“sous-groupe de Sylow H”; “coimage”; “par les relations”',r'Sylow|pro.3|torsion|quotient|class.two|covariance',r'''The margin suggests inertia and Sylow subgroups, while the lower text passes modulo torsion groups on which \(p\) is invertible and sketches a coimage by relations. Which quotient of \(\widehat H(G',M)\) is generated by the indicated conjugation/intersection relations, and which terms of the weakly legible double-coset expression enforce them?''',r'''The pro-3 and class-two words in LM7 E.23/INTAKE LM7_CONTINUED §? provide an arithmetic comparison target, but their excerpted correction modules and fibers are not identified with this Tate quotient; the current scan adds a specific transfer method and a reading question.''',['LM7 E.23','INTAKE LM7_CONTINUED §?'])
add('N068','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','The questioned H1 bijection',[(44,15)],'self-flagged',r'“est bijectif (?)”',r'H.?1|inerti|units|unités|semilocal|semi.local|descent',r'''The proposed map starts with \(H^1(G,O^*)\), restricts to the inertia group, and reduces coefficients to the stated residue units, with an explicit question mark on bijectivity. Its kernel and image must be computed through \(1+\mathfrak m\to O^*\to(O/\mathfrak m)^*\), retaining the semilocal orbit of maximal ideals and the uncertain coefficient notation in the target.''',r'''MPL_131 RN001’s descent lead and MPL_60_036-070 §2’s local norm lead do not contain this H1 map; the current page adds an unresolved units-descent question with its exact source flag.''',['MPL_131 RN001','MPL_60_036-070 §2'],flags=['self'])
add('N069','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','The GL(n) extension question',[(44,19)],'self-flagged',r'“Qu’en est-il dans le cas … des Gl(n,O)”',r'Gl|GL|descent|descente|représent|represent|H.?1',r'''The next sentence asks for an analogue with \(\operatorname{GL}_n(O)\), making matrix cocycles and their change of basis the concrete objects to examine. The map to test is restriction to inertia followed by entrywise reduction, and its fibers concern semilinear rank-\(n\) modules with a specified residual form.''',r'''MPL_131 10/RN001 give a descent programme with earlier locations 131/002 and 131/017, while scan 049 later uses \(H^1(k,\operatorname{GL}_n)=0\); neither the supplied excerpt nor that field calculation proves this semilocal assertion.''',['MPL_131 10','MPL_131 RN001'],flags=['self'])
add('N070','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','The author’s missing noetherian assumptions',[(44,23),(44,40)],'self-flagged',r'“justification par Zariski”; “hyp. … noethériennes … à faire ??”',r'noeth|completion|complét|dense|Greenberg|thickness',r'''The long displayed comparison interchanges completion with Tate cohomology and then invokes a decomposition-group calculation; the annotation explicitly asks which noetherian assumptions are required. The lower diagram adds injectivity and dense images for \(\alpha,\beta\), followed by “on passe au quotient !”, so an assessment must give the module topology, completion maps, and closedness or quotient argument used at that last step.''',r'''MPL_91_099-143 §68 mentions Greenberg–Néron thickness conditions at 91/126 and 91/128 and point/image comparisons only in a truncated lead; the present completion map offers a concrete comparison question but supplies no morphism to those Greenberg objects.''',['MPL_91_099-143 §68'],flags=['self'])
add('N071','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','The two cancelled idèle quotient questions',[(45,9),(45,25)],'self-flagged / withdrawn in the same text',r'“ou un quotient ???”; “ceci est-il … identique à Z_2^{S^\infty} ???”',r'id[èe]le|unramified|ramif|quotient|section|norm',r'''Both explicit quotient questions occur inside the large cancelled block, which links units, global units, real places and abelian Galois groups. The maps that need reconstruction are the inclusion of global units into the specified idèle-unit group and its image in the real-place factor; the written intersections and quotients cannot be replaced by a familiar class-field sequence without checking those maps.''',r'''LM7 E.23 is open for marked arithmetic section maps, while MPL_60_036-070 §2 mentions restricted rational norms; neither excerpt gives this idèle sequence, so the current scan adds a withdrawn arithmetic draft and two unresolved source questions.''',['LM7 E.23','MPL_60_036-070 §2'],flags=['self','withdrawn'])
add('N072','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','The local norm criterion’s domains',[(45,30)],'reading question',r'“N_{L/k}U_L=U_L … N_{L/k}L^*⊃U_k”',r'norm|local|unramified|ramif|unit',r'''The surviving lemma changes “normale” to “extension” and writes \(U_L\) again after the equality, although the norm takes values in \(k^*\), with \(K/k\) also varying in the text. A precise comparison must specify the extension \(k\hookrightarrow L\), the norm \(N_{L/k}:L^*\to k^*\), the chosen valuations and the embeddings of the unit groups before assessing its ramification criterion.''',r'''MPL_60_036-070 §2 gives a restricted rational-norm lead but no complete local norm criterion; these scans add an explicit formula whose fields and target groups require checking.''',['MPL_60_036-070 §2'])
add('N073','H. Trace, inertia, completion, and the cancelled idèle draft','A norm-unit test for the meaning of local field',[(45,30)],'own idea',r'“un corps local … quel”',r'local|norm|ramif|complete|compl',r'''Does “corps local” here exclude the complete discretely valued field \(K=\mathbf C((t))\)? In the explicit extension \(L=\mathbf C((u))\), \(t=u^2\), the ramification index is two, but every \(a(t)\in\mathbf C[[t]]^*\) has a square root \(b(t)\in\mathbf C[[t]]^*\), and its norm as an element of \(K\subset L\) is \(b(t)^2=a(t)\), so \(N_{L/K}U_L=U_K\). This test isolates the residue-field and local-field convention that the draft’s unit criterion must retain.''',r'''The local-symbol/norm excerpts MPL_60_002-035 §2 and MPL_60_036-070 §2 provide no definition of local field, so this is a convention test for the current formula rather than a claimed refutation under every possible intended convention.''',['MPL_60_002-035 §2','MPL_60_036-070 §2'],confidence='high for the explicit Laurent-series calculation; unresolved for the intended convention',reason='The extension and square-root construction are explicit, but the manuscript does not define corps local on this leaf.')
